🔹 1. What is List Interface?
-List is a part of Java Collection Framework.
-It is an interface in java.util package.
-ordered collection of elements (sequence matters).
-Allows duplicate elements.
-Elements can be accessed by index.
-Common implementing classes:
ArrayList (dynamic/resizable growable array internally)
LinkedList (doubly linked list)
Vector (synchronized array, legacy)
Stack (LIFO structure, legacy)

🔹 2. Key Features of List
-Ordered Collection: Maintains insertion order.
-Indexed Access: Access elements using index get(int index).
-Duplicates Allowed: You can store the same element multiple times.
-Dynamic Size: Most implementations like ArrayList grow automatically.
-Null Allowed: Most implementations allow null values (ArrayList, LinkedList), except Vector may differ.
