 va ListIterator Interface
 ListIterator Interface is used to traverse the element in a backward and forward direction.

 ListIterator Interface declaration
 public interface ListIterator<E> extends Iterator<E>

 methods:ListIterator

 | **Method**        | **What it does (Simple Explanation)**                                              |
 | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
 | `add(E e)`        | Adds the specified element to the list.                                            |
 | `hasNext()`       | Returns `true` if there is a next element when moving forward.                     |
 | `next()`          | Returns the next element and moves the cursor forward.                             |
 | `nextIndex()`     | Returns the index of the next element that `next()` would return.                  |
 | `hasPrevious()`   | Returns `true` if there is a previous element when moving backward.                |
 | `previous()`      | Returns the previous element and moves the cursor backward.                        |
 | `previousIndex()` | Returns the index of the element that `previous()` would return.                   |
 | `remove()`        | Removes the last element returned by `next()` or `previous()`.                     |
 | `set(E e)`        | Replaces the last element returned by `next()` or `previous()` with a new element. |
